---
import Layout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Header } from "../components/Header";
---

<Layout>
  <Header currentPath="/work" />
  <main class="min-h-screen px-6 lg:px-12 py-12">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="space-y-12">
        <h1 class="font-mono text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold">work</h1>

        <!--Projects List Container-->
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
          <div
            class="bg-gradient-to-br from-dark-800/50 to-dark-900/50 backdrop-blur-sm border border-dark-700/50 rounded-lg p-6"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
              <div
                class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white/10 flex items-center justify-center"
              >
                <img
                  src="/willow.png"
                  alt="Willow"
                  class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                />
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                <h3 class="text-xl lg:text-2xl font-bold text-white">
                  <a href="https://willow-cdc.github.io/">Willow</a>
                </h3>
                <p class="text-primary-400 font-medium">
                  Software Engineer, Creator
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right text-gray-400 lg:ml-auto">
                <p class="font-medium text-sm lg:text-base">2024</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300">
              <p class="leading-relaxed">
                Worked with a team of four engineers to build an open-source
                framework that keeps a Redis cache in sync with a PostgreSQL
                database in near real-time, without the setup burden of
                assembling a CDC pipeline by hand.
              </p>

              <p>
                Caches go stale. The usual fixes — polling the database,
                invalidating on write, or setting a TTL and hoping — all trade
                correctness for simplicity. Log-based change data capture solves
                it properly by reading the database's write-ahead log, but
                standing one up means wiring together Debezium, Kafka,
                Zookeeper, and Kafka Connect, and getting every piece of that
                configuration right. Willow closes that gap. It's self-hosted,
                so you keep control of your infrastructure and avoid vendor
                lock-in, and its UI walks you through pipeline setup as a series
                of forms — connect a Postgres source, pick the tables and
                columns to capture, point it at a Redis sink. What took nine
                manual steps takes four.

                <p>What I worked on:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    Built the KafkaJS connector that transforms Kafka events and
                    writes them to the cache
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Designed the REST API for pipeline creation and teardown
                    (Express)
                  </li>
                  <li>Built the pipeline management UI (React, Material UI)</li>
                  <li>
                    Tracked down Debezium configuration issues that prevented
                    multiple pipelines from connecting to the same database
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Got Willow running under a least-privilege database user, so
                    it no longer required superuser access
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Co-authored the technical case study on Willow's
                    architecture and design decisions
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="bg-gradient-to-br from-dark-800/50 to-dark-900/50 backdrop-blur-sm border border-dark-700/50 rounded-lg p-6"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
              <div
                class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white/10 flex items-center justify-center"
              >
                <img
                  src="/willow.png"
                  alt="Willow"
                  class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                />
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                <h3 class="text-xl lg:text-2xl font-bold text-white">
                  MP3 Kiosk App and Dashboard
                </h3>
                <p class="text-primary-400 font-medium">
                  Software Engineer, Creator
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right text-gray-400 lg:ml-auto">
                <p class="font-medium text-sm lg:text-base">2025 - Present</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300">
              <p class="leading-relaxed">
                Manage a fleet of MP3 players for a residential treatment
                program. Designed and developed kiosk app for client Android MP3
                devices using device policy restrictions. Developed fleet
                manager dashboard for managing music updates on devices.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="bg-gradient-to-br from-dark-800/50 to-dark-900/50 backdrop-blur-sm border border-dark-700/50 rounded-lg p-6"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
              <div
                class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white/10 flex items-center justify-center"
              >
                <img
                  src="/willow.png"
                  alt="Willow"
                  class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                />
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                <h3 class="text-xl lg:text-2xl font-bold text-white">
                  origin*
                </h3>
                <p class="text-primary-400 font-medium">
                  Software Engineer, Creator
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right text-gray-400 lg:ml-auto">
                <p class="font-medium text-sm lg:text-base">2026</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300">
              <p class="leading-relaxed">
                Developed a RequestBin clone for testing webhooks.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="bg-gradient-to-br from-dark-800/50 to-dark-900/50 backdrop-blur-sm border border-dark-700/50 rounded-lg p-6"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
              <div
                class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white/10 flex items-center justify-center"
              >
                <img
                  src="/willow.png"
                  alt="Willow"
                  class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                />
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                <h3 class="text-xl lg:text-2xl font-bold text-white">
                  BacklogUp
                </h3>
                <p class="text-primary-400 font-medium">
                  Software Engineer, Creator
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right text-gray-400 lg:ml-auto">
                <p class="font-medium text-sm lg:text-base">2026</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300">
              <p class="leading-relaxed">
                Developed a web app for organizing a videogame backlog.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!--Employment List Container-->
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
          <h1 class="font-mono text-2xl text-accent-500">Employment</h1>
          <ul>
            <li>KYUMH, YCA -> CSA</li>
            <li>Asbury Theological Seminary, Custodian</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
